from a shocking major character death to  extra deadly demobats that would have  killed steve and a big change to the  mind flayer reveal in the finale there  were some fascinating moments and scenes  cut from stranger things four yipikai  movie lovers i'm jan and in this video  i'm revealing the deleted scenes and  alternate ending you never got to see in  the fourth season of stranger things  spoilers ahead of course so take care  in the season 4 finale everything goes  horribly wrong when wekner claims max as  his fourth victim opening the four gates  to the upside down although max briefly  died 11 managed to bring her back though  she was left in a coma the duffer  brothers have revealed now however that  in the season's original ending max died  permanently but they changed their minds  about this as they wanted to end on a  little more of a question mark obviously  i'm glad max survived her deadly  encounter and given how much season 4  channels the empire strikes back i think  her comatose state is akin to han solo  ending up frozen in carbonite in other  words it's something she'll surely  recover from in the fifth and final  season  the upside downs demobats introduced in  season four were fearsome predators and  with their hive mind connection to  wekner they could act as the villain  spies fan favorite eddie tragically died  from his injuries after being attacked  by the creatures but originally the  flying monsters were going to be even  more deadly according to stranger things  concept artist michael marjunia the  initially approved version of the bats  had serrated tail tentacles that were  meant to wrap and then cut flesh if the  demo bats we saw in the show had been  equipped with this razor-sharp tail it  seems like they could have easily killed  steve when one of them wrapped its tail  around his neck and began strangling him  after he was taken into the upside down  on top of that another even more  gruesome version of the demo bat was  considered whose head and body would  split open horizontally i think this  design would have felt a little similar  to the demo dogs and demogorgons whose  heads open up although seeing the whole  of the demo bat's body open up would  have been pretty horrifying by the way  the original design for the demo bats  was based on the parasitic minoc bats  from star wars which attacked the  millennium falcon in the empire strikes  back  fans have been heartbroken over the  death of eddie but the season very  nearly ended with another big death as  well as the duffer brothers have  revealed that originally dimitri aka  enzo didn't make it out of the season  alive the russian prison guard became  friends with hopper when they were  imprisoned together after being given up  by the treacherous yori dimitri was  crucial in changing yuri's mind about  sabotaging the helicopter which in turn  ensured hopper joyce and murray could  finally escape the russian prison after  they destroyed the demo dogs and  demogorgon perhaps killing off a russian  good guy felt too similar to alexi dying  at the end of season 3 so the duff has  changed it after all from what we saw in  season 4 there wasn't any major  narrative need to kill off dimitri so  the change feels like a sensible one  it's also possible the duffers still  have a little something planned for a  russian storyline in season five so they  kept him alive given how he told yuri  that russia could be under threat from  the upside down as well  when asked on the happy sad confused  podcast whether eddie was always  destined to have a single season arc on  the show the duffer brothers explained  that even if he had survived his  encounter with the demo bats his  character was still doomed and he would  have wound up in jail because nobody in  hawkins would have accepted a  supernatural explanation for what  happened to chrissy fred and patrick and  he was still being demonized at the end  sadly the duffers said eddie's plan to  finally graduate was never a realistic  one and he was hurtling towards doom  through all of season 4.  an incredible piece of concept art which  sadly didn't make it into the final cut  was of this moment when eleven sends  henry through an inter-dimensional tear  from the rainbow room the point of view  here is from the hellscape that one  falls into and it's a beautiful shot  that would have been fantastic to see  after one was thrown into the hellscape  he arrived in a strange new world where  he came across a swarming mass of dark  particles that were seemingly alive with  his powers he shaped these into the  giant spider form we know as the mind  flayer that he would go on to control  and use to manipulate will and season  two however ma has explained that in  early concepts of that scene in order to  create the mind player one actually had  to extract the particles out of floating  boulders by contrast the final show  reveals that the particles already  existed at a separate entity before  henry ever went into that dimension the  upside down has probably been around for  thousands of years millions i wouldn't  be surprised if it predated a dinosaur  and that change might also imply that  the particles in this dimension as well  as the demogorgon creatures which were  already living there when henry arrived  weren't malicious until he came along  and transformed them into malevolent  force for his own ends concept artist ma  also revealed that the floating rocks in  this dimension are an asteroid field  operating under an altered state of  gravity and his initial idea was that  the mind flayer particles were an  anti-gravity element that would lift the  boulders into the air making the rocks  fall upwards this sounds like the  particles that one discovers are a kind  of fundamental force that governs things  in this other dimension apparently the  idea was abandoned at the end as ma says  that it would have taken too long to  explain in the context of the story also  the dimension's original look in this  concept art was a lot darker whereas it  had a yellowish orange hue and lighting  in the final version  and wekner's mind layer where he  torments max in eleven and stores the  bodies of his victims originally had  some strikingly different designs  according to ma this one is a large  vortex where fragments of the house were  dissolving along with spires containing  rotted victims everything would have  been moving slowly swirling in a  circular motion and in this version of  the villain's lair wekner dragged his  victims across a blood-soaked space  towards a huge stone structure in the  background mara said that this idea and  the look of the mind layer in general is  influenced by the paintings of the  dystopian surrealist polish artist  bekzinski and this similar shot of a  vast landscape with wekner dragging his  victim to a towering slab of rock on top  of an enormous mound was inspired by the  sci-fi psychological thrill of the cell  which features scenes literally entering  a killer's twisted mind and dreamscape  in this other horrifying version there's  a slimy web of interconnected vines  suspending three of wechner's victims  over some kind of altar and it looks  like he was dragging his fourth victim  over to the spot there's a real spider's  web feel about this design which is  fitting of course given henry's love of  black widow spiders as a child and in  these earlier versions max was suspended  in the air via vechna's vines rather  than against a column as happened in the  show this is more akin to how vechner  himself levitates via a web of vines  whenever he's projecting his  consciousness outside his physical body  by the way ma also revealed that the  swirling haze in wekner's lair is meant  to reference the storm in billy's mind  that eleven saw when she reached into  his memories in season three and an  early concept of wekner's attic had him  lifted into the air by vines coming  mostly from the floor this later morphed  into the final idea where he was  suspended instead from the sides and the  ceiling deliberately creating the effect  of a spider's web and how a spider waits  in its web to trap its victims it's a  very creepy moment when fred has a  hallucination of grieving mourners at a  funeral and a little girl points at him  and her finger extends into a long  deformed claw similar to one of vechna's  giant fingers but this original concept  art suggests the moment could have been  even more gruesome with tentacles also  emerging from the girl's arm and across  her hand and blood streaming from her  eyes and if you'd like to discover the  super creepy horrifying designs for  vechna that we almost got including one  where he had four legs and a mantis-like  body tap here to watch that video or  there's a link in the video description  so movie lovers what do you think about  these original ideas for season four let  me know in the comments below  if you liked this video do leave a  thumbs up i really appreciate it bitchin  right and you can tap left to discover  every incredible easter egg you missed  in the final part of season 4. thanks  for enjoying stranger things with me and  hope you have a marvelous movie loving  week yippee kai review lovers
 

